 ## Surface normal-map activation
 
-- `surface_normal_maps` stays opt-in. BasicMaterial supports supplemental maps on authored FVF3/FVF4 tangents and generated FVF3/FVF4 geometry from VMesh NORMAL+TEX1/TEX2. Preserve MAT-owned `NmName`. DFM uses per-corner generated tangents with Basic-Skinned; skinned PBR and additional PBR channels remain unsupported. Release the temporary GPU lease after each draw and restore texture slot 2.
+- `surface_normal_maps` and `surface_pbr_maps` stay independent and opt-in. BasicMaterial supports supplemental normal maps on authored FVF3/FVF4 tangents and generated FVF3/FVF4 geometry from VMesh NORMAL+TEX1/TEX2. Preserve MAT-owned `NmName`, `RtName`, and `MtName`. Supplemental roughness and metallic maps use PBR slots 4 and 3 with the configured UV channel; scalar values multiply their maps or provide map-free PBR values. Keep DFM on the skinned Basic path; skinned PBR remains unsupported. Release each temporary GPU lease after its draw and restore the touched texture slots.
 - Keep `SurfaceNormalMapsEnabled` synchronized from GameSettings at startup and at every live settings apply. Turning it off retires unused GPU cache entries through the fence queue.
+- Keep `SurfacePbrMapsEnabled` synchronized from GameSettings at startup and every live settings apply. The `surface_pbr_maps` config entry and `--render-surface-pbr-maps=on|off` override control supplemental roughness and metallic maps only. Turning it off retires unused GPU cache entries through the fence queue.
 
